!!! A statement normally ends at end of line. ';' ends one explicitly, so
!!! several short statements can share a line -- the cheaper spelling when
!!! the statements are trivial and token count matters.
area demo.terminator

main returns number begin function
    variable a as number is 0; variable b as number is 0; variable c as number is 0
    set a to 1; set b to 2; set c to a plus b
    say a; say b; say c

    !!! A trailing ';' on a single statement is allowed and means nothing.
    say "done";

    give 0
end function
